# .dockerignore -- portal build. Context = bifrost-platform/bifrost-portal/
#
# This context is already a single app directory, so a deny-all floor is not needed to make
# it minimal. What IS needed is to keep two specific things out, both of which would
# otherwise be copied by the `COPY src/` + `COPY public/` lines or by a future `COPY . .`:

# 1. A previous build output committed at the app root. Vite emits to dist/, so these are
#    stale. Harmless in the build stage; in the serve stage they would shadow the fresh
#    bundle and the portal would serve an old index.html with a dead asset hash.
assets/
vite.svg

# 2. Anything a local dev loop leaves behind.
node_modules/
dist/
.git/
*.log
*.bak
*.bak-*
*-bak
*_fixed.jsx
*_v2.jsx
patch-*.py
patch_*.py

# Not needed in the image, and README.md is the stock Vite template text.
README.md
.gitignore

# NOTE: public/vite.svg IS copied (index.html references /vite.svg as the favicon). The
# `vite.svg` line above excludes only the stray copy at the APP ROOT, because in
# .dockerignore a bare pattern does not cross `/` -- it does not touch public/vite.svg.
# That distinction is load-bearing: the same `*` -does-not-cross-/` rule is what made 18
# of the router's 63 unexcluded backup files slip through its .dockerignore.
